# gate-registry.yml.ejs — the DECLARATIVE gate registry (#2041, AC-2041.4).
#
# Every gate the generated check-all.mjs runs is declared here: id, display
# name, lane level, kind, and spawn command. The generator
# (src/generators/check-all.ts) renders this manifest with the project config
# (EJS expressions in `cmd` resolve at generation time), validates the shape,
# and consumes it to emit the gate sections of check-all.mjs — replacing the
# hardcoded runCheck(...) calls that used to live inline in the template.
#
# Entry fields:
#   id         kebab-case identifier — used by `--gate <id>` and the layering
#              contract test (scripts/test-gate-layering.mjs).
#   name       display name (the runCheck first argument; also accepted by
#              `--gate <name>` for backward compatibility with #2078).
#   level      L1 | L2 | L3 — the lane this gate belongs to. Structural
#              containment L1 ⊂ L2 ⊂ L3: `check-all.mjs <level>` runs every
#              gate whose level is <= the requested level.
#   kind       check (hard) | warn (advisory) | tool (CI-aware) | inline
#              (custom JS body in the template, declared here for manifest
#              completeness — see the INLINE_BLOCKS section of check-all.mjs).
#   cmd        [binary, ...args] — EJS expressions are allowed; rendered at
#              generation time (e.g. `<%%= packageManager %>`).
#   language   optional — wraps the gate in `if (language === '<lang>')`.
#   condition  optional — raw expression wrapped in `if (<expr>) { ... }`.
#   else       optional — raw body emitted in the `else` branch (used by the
#              SKIP-report gates: audit, npm-ci drift, playwright rules).
#   soft       true → the gate runs with `{ soft: graceActive }`.
#   promotes_to  optional — id of a gate this one REPLACES at runtime once its
#              own level is reached (e.g. an L3 `harness-full` entry with
#              `promotes_to: harness-fast` skips `harness-fast` once the run
#              level is L3+). #9003.
#   audit      optional true — an audit-only gate, a second axis orthogonal
#              to level; skipped at runtime when the consumer sets
#              `ARBITER_AUDIT_MODE=off`. #9003.
#
# ORDER IS MEANINGFUL: the emitted script runs gates in registry order within
# each level (the pre-#2041 inline order is preserved).
#
# Existing Code Survey (CANON-16): the de-facto registry was the inline
# runCheck(...) surface of check-all.mjs.ejs (191 calls) — no separate registry
# file existed; this manifest REPLACES that inline surface (justified by
# AC-2041.4), it does not duplicate it.

